{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1091656-under-a-blood-red-moon-2017","id":1091656,"title":"Under a Blood Red Moon (2017)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-12T12:17:23-07:00","id":1091656,"title":"Under a Blood Red Moon (2017)","content":"Hey guys,<br /> <br /> I'm going to be running Under a Blood Red Moon as a campaign for my new pack of players as their first werewolf game and I'm trying to figure out ways of modifying the story and updating it. Also, any suggestions which people might have for improving it. I think it's a fairly solid story right out of the gate personally if (perhaps) a bit combat heavy.<br /> <br /> Anyone have any experiences with the game or suggestions for making it better?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T15:38:36-07:00","id":1091730,"title":"","content":"<u><b>My Problems with Under a Blood Red Moon</b></u><br /> <br /> 1. <b>Abomination are stupid:</b> I'm inclined to think it's an inherently unsalvageable concept and it would be better just to state the two species can't crossbreed. However, I like the idea of the Harold Goodston. Basically, SOME guy who is completely beyond the pale of Garou society who wants back in. I'm curious what to replace his &quot;thing&quot; with.<br /> <br /> I have a couple of ideas:<br /> <br /> A. Harold is a somehow-sane Black Spiral Dancer who wants to repent.<br /> B. Harold is a member of the Skin Dancers tribe.<br /> C. Harold is actually Samuel Haight with a complete personality change or maybe he's playing the role of the repentant were to get close to them.<br /> <br /> 2. <b>Gulfora the Succubus</b>: Obviously, this is another crossover issue as a Christian demon doesn't really fit the Garou mythos. I'm inclined to think of just substituting an Enticer Formori into the story but if so, is she an independent Formori or is it Pentex behind it or what? Would another kind of spirit manifesting be better? Or perhaps a Black Spiral Dancer who just happens to be extremely attractive (illusions?)<br /> <br /> 3. <b>Corrupting Jupiter</b>: I actually like the idea of corrupting a Totem but the whole Jupiter Sept seems very out of step with later cosmology, especially since Celestines are so far removed from daily affairs. What would be a good Totem to substitute? Grandfather Thunder? If so, would that REALLY make the Shadow Lords furious about all this? What about another Totem? Maybe it's about summoning Eater of Souls or some other figure through an Anchor-Point.<br /> <br /> What's the Maguffin?<br /> <br /> 4. <b>Vampires and Weres going to War</b>: The premise depends on the Sabbat and Black Spiral Dancers teaming up to take the Jupiter Sept with the Garou blaming vampires in general for it. However, that depends on a lot of ignorance of the Garou about vampires as well as the assumption no one would think to check a little deeper.<br /> <br /> Also, there's the problem in the game the Gangrel and Garou make a truce which seems like would at least be someone pointing out vampires have NO knowledge of the Spirit World so they can't be involved or it's a different group of vampires involved in the war. Yes, I know that means I have a problem with the basic premise but I'd prefer to shore it up rather than throw it away completely. Maybe the King of the Silver Fangs (Jacob Morningstar?) thinks it's a good idea, I dunno?<br /> <br /> Why the war and why now?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-12-2017, 06:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T15:55:57-07:00","id":1091738,"title":"","content":"You could have Gulfora be just another monster like a skull pig or thunderwyrm, though obviously in a more socially-presentable form.<br /> <br /> Jupiter has a related Incarna, Zarok, who rules over the planetary realm in the Aetherial. That would be the most immediate one to come to mind.<br /> <br /> As for the war... honestly, it would seem like a much more reasonable approach if vampire occultists (Tremere, for example's sake) somehow got access to the location and started twisting and pulling knobs, so to speak. This would obviously result in the Tremere being murdered horribly, but might not assuage the curiosity in whatever chantry sent them, so they start playing politics in order to engineer everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T16:17:02-07:00","id":1091749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1091656-under-a-blood-red-moon-2017?p=1091738#post1091738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could have Gulfora be just another monster like a skull pig or thunderwyrm, though obviously in a more socially-presentable form.<br /> <br /> Jupiter has a related Incarna, Zarok, who rules over the planetary realm in the Aetherial. That would be the most immediate one to come to mind.<br /> <br /> As for the war... honestly, it would seem like a much more reasonable approach if vampire occultists (Tremere, for example's sake) somehow got access to the location and started twisting and pulling knobs, so to speak. This would obviously result in the Tremere being murdered horribly, but might not assuage the curiosity in whatever chantry sent them, so they start playing politics in order to engineer everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>In this Post Game of Thrones world, I'm also inclined to think the plot needs a few more twists and turns to keep things going. Like maybe the Garou Kings knew the Sabbat were involved but felt this was a good time to clear out the city of Leeches for their own personal gain or prejudices.<br /> <br /> Also, potentially the Tremere manipulated this themselves and are using it to study Garou magic in action.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T18:44:41-07:00","id":1091789,"title":"","content":"Here are some things to think about. However, I will say that I haven't read UBRM in decades so I don't know how appropriate they are to your details.<br /> <br /> 1) The Abomination - Can you use a Kinfolk who was embraced?<br /> <br /> 2) I don't see why a Succubus would present a problem? I always assumed that Garou and the other game lines would always classify creatures according to how they understand that. So Garou wouldn't think Gulfora is a &quot;Christian demon&quot;, they would think she's some powerful Bane in service to the Maeljin Incarna of Lust.<br /> <br /> 3) The Chicago Fanum is supposed to be a center of occultists and Native American artifacts and legends, right? You could use Thunderbird. It is a fairly important mythological figure among Native Americans and should fit well with various aspects of Jupiter.<br /> <br /> 4) You could have a sleeper agent among either the Camarilla or Garou who want the fight to happen so that the plan goes off. A vampire advisor to Lodin who is really a Sabbat infiltrator would work. You could even have an influential Garou planning to defect to the BSDs if you need someone on the other side. As for the &quot;truce&quot;, it is possible that someone powerful on the vampire side (say Inyanaga of the Gangrel or even Menele) is recognized by the local Garou as some kind of important figure, dangerous but friendly, which they haven't realized is actually a vampire. That figure could then give advice/premonition/etc. that to properly succeed, they should accept the offer of a truce by one of the vampire groups (which is then made by a subordinate, protecting their identity). Both characters are fairly knowledgable about a lot of things, so their awareness of the spirit world shouldn't be an issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T01:29:27-07:00","id":1091865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1091656-under-a-blood-red-moon-2017?p=1091789#post1091789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here are some things to think about. However, I will say that I haven't read UBRM in decades so I don't know how appropriate they are to your details.<br /> <br /> 1) The Abomination - Can you use a Kinfolk who was embraced?</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with that is Kinfolk are far enough from Gaian society and not &quot;werewolf&quot; that I imagine most Garou would just consider him to be gutted while they could probably adjust better to being a vampire. I'm leaning toward Skindancer because they're an underused (for obvious reasons) type of character and the horror of what they are when revealed would be interesting. I can also tie it to the Tremere perhaps by having them having helped Haight create the ritual as he was canonically a ghoul for awhile as Kinfolk. I like Haight as a character right up until he became a Mage then deserved to be an ashtray.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) I don't see why a Succubus would present a problem? I always assumed that Garou and the other game lines would always classify creatures according to how they understand that. So Garou wouldn't think Gulfora is a &quot;Christian demon&quot;, they would think she's some powerful Bane in service to the Maeljin Incarna of Lust. </div> </div> </div>True, I suppose it's the desire to incorporate more Werewolf lore and make it feel like it should fit into the setting rather than just be a big huge Crisis on Infinite Earths/Secret Wars crossover.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3) The Chicago Fanum is supposed to be a center of occultists and Native American artifacts and legends, right? You could use Thunderbird. It is a fairly important mythological figure among Native Americans and should fit well with various aspects of Jupiter. </div> </div> </div>That's a very good choice. Alternatively, I could go for broke and have the Sept's importance be not corrupting something but the BSD planning to bring something THROUGH the gates. If I want to be historical, I might have them attempting to do the same ritual which brought Eater-of-Souls through to Roanoke.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4) You could have a sleeper agent among either the Camarilla or Garou who want the fight to happen so that the plan goes off. A vampire advisor to Lodin who is really a Sabbat infiltrator would work. You could even have an influential Garou planning to defect to the BSDs if you need someone on the other side. As for the &quot;truce&quot;, it is possible that someone powerful on the vampire side (say Inyanaga of the Gangrel or even Menele) is recognized by the local Garou as some kind of important figure, dangerous but friendly, which they haven't realized is actually a vampire. That figure could then give advice/premonition/etc. that to properly succeed, they should accept the offer of a truce by one of the vampire groups (which is then made by a subordinate, protecting their identity). Both characters are fairly knowledgable about a lot of things, so their awareness of the spirit world shouldn't be an issue. </div> </div> </div>In fact, Lodin's Seneschal IS a Sabbat infiltrator. Ed Neally could indeed be a character who runs interference to press the Camarilla into war against the Garou in hopes of weakening the city for Sabbat takeover (maybe he makes it seem like the werewolves have allied with the Sabbat or that they're breaking the Masquerade openly and need to be punished). There's a couple of times the werewolves are forced to interact with vampires in the story or potentially can with Al Capone and Kevin Jackson who could explain the truth of the matter to them. If a PC ends up enslaved by Gulfora, she might also reveal this.<br /> <br /> Or, as you say, Inyanga potentially.<br /> <br /> On the werewolf side of things, I have two ideas for potential people pressing the Garou to War.<br /> <br /> 1. An insane Uktena Bane Tender who believes the Garou can be united against the threat in the Farnum (be it a corrupted Thunderbird or Eater of Souls) and that he has been giving deliberately misleading visions and lies to manipulate events.<br /> <br /> 2. A rank 5 Silver Fang who was kidnapped, tortured, and brutalized by vampires for a while when he was a cub and holds a continuing everlasting hatred of them. He and his faction may be involved in the Garou/Kindred war in Milwaukee (why there's one doesn't matter, just the local septs kill vampires and vice versa).<br /> Between the both of them, what starts as a specific problem gets out of the way to become a desire to &quot;cleanse the city.&quot;<br /> <br /> I may even make it clear the idea of all vampires being involved in the city is idiotic but anyone who challenges the idea risks Renown as it's gotten traction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T10:01:53-07:00","id":1091992,"title":"","content":"If you want the &quot;Abomination&quot; character to be a Garou, you could always make him a Ronin who got involved in some dark Bane pacts to learn Gifts (perhaps some BSD totem Gifts as out of tribe), but pulled back from actually joining the BSDs because he realized they were all nuts. Nevertheless, perhaps the Garou think he did join after being disgraced with whatever it was that he did (perhaps mating with another Garou, questioning basic Garou values or beliefs, falling in love with a vampire and saving her from a pack), etc. After being on his journey alone and exploring things, he's now come to realize the Garou were right about things and wants to make amends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T10:25:32-07:00","id":1091998,"title":"","content":"I've done running it 2 months ago. it was second time I did it, this time it is a part of large campaign. I Suggest You to think about it as a bag of ideas connected around plot. I've reshaped it a lot. Fell free to use any of these ideas - my players loved it. First - prophecy. I've created a fallen garou from Children of Gaia - Slayer of phropecies. He was a grand grand child of garou who had vision described in the book. His role was to stop it but he was coward in his heart and the Wyrm found a hole for corruption. He became main antagonist who wanted prophecy to be twisted. He danced the spiral and c\u0142imbed the ladder of leadership in Chicago hive. He had few visions and a knowledge about what might happen. Some sort of future insight , garou Lore knowledge, and correct omen reading. So when the gathering of garou relaxed before war moot in the racoon caern his minions including horribly mutated cannon fooder from insanely filthy hives, sabbat Leeches, fomori and more San\u0119 BSD appeared with silver. The slaughter was great All of gathered died. And then players arrived. Second war party was created this time players as leaders. Soon other characters appeared but the time was running , garou Numbers were small and they had to use All of contacts , resources, allies and other things to call as many garou as they could. I've created other antagonist. Nephandi mage who was too involved in slaughter and was interested in other prophecy - the perfect metis. She was manipulating garou genes taking role of doctor in DNA facility experimanting on cubs before first change. My players wanted to kill her cause she made a nasty move against them. She mixed dna of black fury and wendigo players characters and impregnated fury speeding up child growth . After confrontation with players who tried to rescue a cub who survived massacre in racoon sept (police didn't stop journalists from discovering what happened in sept) fury gived birth to a metis cub - no deformity ( it will be mental) and had problem - breaking a litany and child in time of full scale war. Second - I've made a lot of choices - important. Example - call from Albrecht ( my players love him) we atack the airport - scenario from adventure. All right they go, but travelling there they see a pack of BSD trying to do something bad behaving carefully. Players chose to ignore airport and so they found that Glass walkers two packs stayed away from war for high price. It was important because when leeches minions arrested kinfolk (mega caged many of them - I love new book of wyrm!) only Glass walkers had resources to help them. Of course airport battle went wrong without players and they had to face Albrecht fury. Decisions - it made the fast paced session better. My advice - use it. Every option important with consequences. Thirt thing - let them win. Let players win but make it hard to survive. My players succeed but it cost them a lot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T03:08:25-07:00","id":1092285,"title":"","content":"Oh and of course abomination. I've read somewhere that Goodkin followed Leech as minion or turned to Wyrm. I resigned from making him helpful/tragic character, I made him loyal executioner devoted to serve his undead masters. I made a teenage pack, Smart kids that had to fight in war few days after rite of passage. They were very helpful, knew the city, they started to make her own legend. And bang! After players killed influential leech, Harold handler released the leash and abomination slaughtered and dried young pack out of blood. My players didn't get him and he will return soon, much more evil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T00:38:13-07:00","id":1092689,"title":"","content":"<b>Revised under a Blood Red Moon part 1</b><br /> <br /> Okay, here's my rough idea for the story. It will include a big change to the story to tie into the Croatan and Roanoke.<br /> <br /> 1. The <b>Black Spiral Dancers</b> working with a sect of <b>Sabbat Infernalists </b>massacre the population of the <b>Farnum </b>and proceed to start corrupting the caern/Anchorhead to become a Wyrm caern with atrocities. They also break the Masquerade/Veil in many locations which is part of the second part of the plan. <b>Ed Neally</b>, working as advisor to Prince Lodin, has him blame the werewolves and create a story which the werewolves are working with the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> The Infernalists have many Banes summoned around<b> Lodin </b>and begin drugging his vessels (Ventrue!) which Neally has access to with <b>Pentex </b>provided products designed to up his paranoia. They also have his mistress, Lorraine, targeted which the PCs will eventually find as the Sabbat send him threatening notes claiming they have werewolf allies. Lodin, not in the best of shape, proceeds to declare war on Chicago's werewolves with many names provided by Ed Neally through his Sabbat contacts (who get them from the BSD and their allies in Pentex). Several werewolves, kinfolk, and allies are killed in the resulting massacre.<br /> <br /> 2. The BSD and Sabbat are running at cross purposes during this mission or at least most of the Sabbat. The BSD are planning to use the Farnum, the massacre of many humans, and war to try to summon an aspect of the Wyrm into reality. They're hoping for<b> Eater-Of-Souls</b> but are okay with something less impressive. The fact some <b>Croatan</b> kinfolk escaped to Chicago and became part of the Uktena involved in the Farnum makes the thing all deliciously symbolic in the BSD's minds. They and their infernalist allies are hoping for a full-on &quot;end of the world&quot; time of judgement scenario.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat, by contrast, are painfully ignorant about the whole infernalism/apocalypse angle and just think they're involved in a Garou tribal conflict. They think they're using the BSD and that they can take the city while Lodin is having his mental breakdown.<br /> <br /> 3. I'm going to change the character of <b>Harold Goodston</b> to throw a surprise at my PCs since a couple of them have played this campaign before. In this version, Harold Goodston was a Shadow Lord kinfolk/Puritan in 1600s England and a noted vampire hunter. He eventually got embraced by the Tremere and this drove him insane as he felt abandoned by Gaia as well as damned by his own kinfolk. He either studied the Wyrm ritual at Roanoke extensively or may have even been peripherially involved. He's also the one directing the BSD and Sabbat infernalists.<br /> <br /> The thing is, Harold is actually a Wild Card rather than the seeming Wyrm cultist everyone assumes him to be. Harold has the insane idea that if he summons a suitably powerful Wyrm spirit that the Garou will unite against it as well as destroy the Black Spiral Dancers as a tribe (since a decent chunk of North America's will be there). He also is a megalomaniac enough that if it DOES start the apocalypse, it will save the world from the Wyrm as he believes Gaia will intervene somehow. He's confused his Garou and Christian theology considerably.<br /> <br /> As such, he'll inform the PCs about what's going on &quot;his&quot; side several times. As a Sabbat Inquisitor (ironic), Harold also has access to Vicissitude and Protean so he can simulate a crude mockery of Crinos form.<br /> <br /> 4. On the Garou end, this is actually a much bigger deal than one city in America as all the seers predict something BIG is happening. The PCs being assigned vampire hunting duties is not actually meant to be the primary vanguard of the war as <b>King Albretch</b> is going to be working to destroy all the Black Spiral Dancers in the city that he can who have been raising hell plus trying to retake the Farnum. Vampire-hunting is a secondary front of the war as Lodin is just causing all manner of interference with their attempts to deal with what may be a massive Wyrm infestation (but no one knows how big).<br /> <br /> It's only while they're hunting vampires that they may stumble on what's really going on.<br /> <br /> 5. On the vampire end of things, from their perspective, things are suddenly a lot more insane than their used to. Hundreds of citizens are going missing, &quot;riots&quot; are happening everywhere that they're struggling to overcome, and they're trying to keep the National Guard OUT rather than getting called in. Only about halfway through the adventure do they clue into the fact the Sabbat are involved and immediately go on a war footing. Most vampires want nothing to do with Lodin's declared Blood Hunt on the city's werewolves even as he's brought in outside Archons and contractors (burning every favor he has) to do fighting--including allying with Anarchs.<br /> <br /> Quite a few vampires are just hunkering down or realizing they should get the hell out of the city.<br /> <br /> 6. Because the Garou's worst enemy is themselves, I want to create a Rank 5 (maybe 6) Garou of the Get of Fenris, Shadow Lords, or Silver Fangs to thoroughly screw the pooch. Someone just underneath Albretch and a legendary vampire hunter who comes down to join Albretch's Crusade before immediately diverting large amounts of resources to fight on fronts other than the Farnum. <b>Kills-The-Dead</b> is an old as dirt Garou with a Grand Klaive or Silver Sword who wants to go out in the blaze of glory and sees this as his best chance of doing so. He was a former friend of Jacob Morningkill during his saner days and absolutely disrespects Albretch but has enough pull to throw his work into disarray. Kills-The-Dead is starting to have the typical Silver Fang madness in delusions of grandeur in his old age and believes if he DOESN'T die he might become King and lead the Garou on a purge even greater than Albretch's of the Seventh Generation--cleansing the continent of vampires (if not the world).<br /> <br /> I may make him the head of the Silver Pack, too, making an opening when they all get killed in the end.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-17-2017, 06:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T01:30:36-07:00","id":1092693,"title":"","content":"Very interesting story. I'd love to read part 2. Few questions:<br /> 1. Would You run the adventure on rpol? I'd love to play!<br /> 2. Would You put in it some BSD hive leader with much more interesting background then in original adventure? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T01:46:23-07:00","id":1092697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werewolf43</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1091656-under-a-blood-red-moon-2017?p=1092693#post1092693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Very interesting story. I'd love to read part 2. Few questions:<br /> 1. Would You run the adventure on rpol? I'd love to play!<br /> 2. Would You put in it some BSD hive leader with much more interesting background then in original adventure?</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Alas, it'll be with my home group but I'll share the details for anyone who wants to hear about them.<br /> <br /> 2. I'm not sure there's any point the PCs will meet a BSD other than &quot;Grr, slash&quot; but I do think this should involve a massive commitment from the BSD so one should definitely be represented.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T03:36:40-07:00","id":1092723,"title":"","content":"That's sad. I hoped for some play. I'd like to read aout what happened in Your session.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T03:07:06-07:00","id":1093594,"title":"","content":"<b>Under a Blood Red Moon part 2</b><br /> <br /> Here's my rough outline so far for what is rapidly becoming a campaign.<br /> <br /> <b>Act One: The Road to Chicago</b><br /> <br /> 1. The PCs will head to a gas station where they will end up accidentally encountering a <b>Sabbat pack</b> as they're making some shovel heads. Not caring about making the Sabbat &quot;badass&quot;, I'm going to have them flee on motorcycles with the shovel-heads left behind and insane with hunger. Of course, the PCs are unlikely to help them and will most likely slaughter them but they're actually innocents in all of this. The police will also arrive and while they can be driven off by Crinos form, if the PCs don't sabotage their cameras in the car, they'll have violated the veil.<br /> <br /> Note: We did this section last night and it went quite well. I had <b>Harold Goodston </b>as one of the Sabbat pack and talk to them about his plans before he fled with Mist form like a coward.<br /> <br /> 2. The PCs will arrive at a massive moot outside of Chicago at a really-really overcrowded local sept that looks a bit like werewolf Woodstock. <b>King Albretch</b> has summoned as many wolves as were willing to make it to North America and there may well be a 1000 of them present with more possibly to follow. The PCs will have some chance to move around and experience Garou culture separate from homid.<br /> <br /> Some encounters I have planned are:<br /> <br /> * Finding out the Garou have taken a bunch of police and local farmers in the area hostage at a house because they investigated. Some drunken angry Garou want to slaughter them all to protect the Litany.<br /> * The PCs encountering a Kinfolk woman who escaped her abusive husband with a new lover, only to find the &quot;higher-ranked&quot; Garou is also at the moot.<br /> * Some chance to deal with tribes they don't normally meet like Stargazers and an all Bonegnawer pack.<br /> * A Glass Walker selling talens for cash money and then getting called out for it.<br /> * Possibly a delegation of Shifters which are VERY uncomfortable here.<br /> * A very drunk and attractive female Garou will want to seduce one of the male PCs in violation of the Litany because this thing is actually fairly common at moots. It's just a terrible place for it.<br /> <br /> 3. Albretch will then call them to speak privately, explain they're going to do some vampire hunting and that he wants this to go as smoothly as possible. His enemies are the Black Spiral Dancers and retaking the <b>Farnum</b>. He doesn't want this to explode. It's a plan which promptly goes to hell when <b>Kills-the-Dead </b>shows up and gives a speech about cleansing New York City along with exterminating all of the undead that rouses everyone to action.<br /> <br /> 4. Politics wise, the PCs can play around a bit as the Shadow Lords will be willing to help them with some of the above encounters if they're willing to agree to favors. They're encouraging the conflict between Albretch and Kills the Dead because they want to weaken his position politically. On the other hand, they actually are fairly good at getting people working on consensus and will surprisingly back down if the players make an argument that disrupting Albretch's plans actually would hurt the Garou nation as a whole.<br /> <br /> 5. At the end of the moot, the PCs are assigned to go visit a Kinfolk family, pick up the information on the vampires, and go slaying. That will be part of Act II, however, before everything completely goes to hell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-17-2017, 06:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T04:06:34-07:00","id":1093606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1091656-under-a-blood-red-moon-2017?p=1093594#post1093594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Under a Blood Red Moon part 2</b><br /> <br /> <br /> * The PCs encountering a Kinfolk woman who escaped her abusive husband with a new lover, only to find the &quot;higher-ranked&quot; Garou is also at the moot.<br /> * A Glass Walker selling talens for cash money and then getting called out for it.<br /> * A very drunk and attractive female Garou will want to seduce one of the male PCs in violation of the Litany because this thing is actually fairly common at moots. It's just a terrible place for it.<br /> <br /> 4. Politics wise, the PCs can play around a bit as the Shadow Lords will be willing to help them with some of the above encounters if they're willing to agree to favors. They're encouraging the conflict between Albretch and Kills the Dead because they want to weaken his position politically. On the other hand, they actually are fairly good at getting people working on consensus and will surprisingly back down if the players make an argument that disrupting Albretch's plans actually would hurt the Garou nation as a whole.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This is in my opinion the best part. Drunk girl - I did it in Fianna moot and worked, But I see the first and second first time and it's brilliant.<br /> And Shadow Lords. My beloved tribe, second only to Red Talons. I think that American Lords don't have resources and guts to dig under Albrecht. They would only piss him off. But there are the other more reckless garou, ideal for the role of pawns in the paws of Lords. If I may leave a suggestion (I don't want to offend You, think that Your plot idea is very good): if You'd like to use a character who would be careless use Arne Guth Stormbright - he have a nazi metis child (Pink Tom) with Bladetooth, he could be blackmailed by Lords. And as I remember he wanted to do everything to hush the case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T23:13:52-07:00","id":1095380,"title":"","content":"I recommend the Storm Eater as a Replacement for Jupiter/Zarok.<br /> <br /> <br /> Demons are no problem for Garou Cosmology they know spirits have odd conflicting histories and lie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T00:52:19-07:00","id":1095400,"title":"","content":"Semitic Demons in WtA could simply be wayward servants of the Patriarch incarna. If they are supposed to behave like Fallen, just allow them to burrow their way into mortal shells.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars